{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>יפליא.</b> He shall set apart and declare." "<b>בערכך נפשות.</b> The sense: that one may vow, saying, 'If HaShem does such-and-such for me, I will redeem myself according to my valuation, or my child's valuation, or an animal's valuation.' And the kaf in בערכך is, according to all the grammarians, superfluous; the sense is 'according to a valuation.' Some say the kaf is for addressing the priest, and they explain כערכך הכהן as 'like your valuation, O priest.' They call this the heh of address, and they say about הערכך that it is a strange form, like בתוך האהלי — and in my opinion that means 'my tent.' So too הערכך: 'your valuation.'" "And the sense of <b>נפשות.</b> A general term for person and animal."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {1 "Resolved ה״א יקרא לו ה״א הקריאה as 'the heh of address,' a standard grammatical category (ה' הקריאה/ה' הפנייה); the manuscript abbreviation הקריא׳ is expanded accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:58.538366049Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}